  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Story_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a62bb9a7cc3667f4f9bf562f73fa4966, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 14436339712
    m_Localized: " Henry is a young man who works as a handyman in a city flooded
      by crime. Every day, he attends one of his clients\u2019 houses to fix something.
      His life is a constant routine: he goes to work, gets paid, buys something
      to improve his craft, and returns home. But Henry has a gentle heart and a
      wild and clever mind, and he\u2019d love to see his city thrive.\n \n Today
      he\u2019s attending an annual mandatory plumbing workshop at the National University
      of Repairmanshift that he needs to fulfill to keep his license. Everything
      seems to be quite boring, as usual\u2026"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 18096689057792
    m_Localized: " Henry went to bed with his heart pounding the previous night.
      He had just killed a man, and he was navigating a rollercoaster of emotions.
      The room spun around him. He did not feel guilty nor shamed. He felt empowered,
      enraged. He felt he was doing the right thing, but his body was shivering.\n
      \n That note he found on the guy\u2019s body, that guy who was related to one
      of his clients. Something inside of him ignited, he needed to find out more
      about this and try to stop that crime.\n \n Today was going to be a long day\u2026"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 18134462959616
    m_Localized: " Now it was obvious. Henry enjoyed fighting crime and cleaning
      his city of these pests. But he needed to keep going and defeat as many criminals
      as possible to try to get rid of all the criminal networks in town.\n \n He
      was exhausted again, fighting criminals was a heavy exercise, but he was starting
      his new day with a lot of prospects in mind\u2026"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 233293047468032
    m_Localized: Fixer Herald
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 233521918054400
    m_Localized: Are vigilantes our only hope?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 233584966832128
    m_Localized: "A young man prevented a robbery from taking place last night, when
      he decided to fight against a robber and ended up killing him. The young man
      ran away from the place looking disturbed according to witnesses. \n \n The
      identity of the robber was later identified as Ricky Mandino, a distant relative
      of one of the wealthiest families in the city. The family denied commenting,
      but sources closest to them tell us they denied even knowing that person was
      in town.\n \n According to some witnesses, the young man who prevented the
      crime was dressed in worker clothes and hit him with a wooden hammer. This
      makes the police believe that this aspiring vigilante was coming from the National
      University of Repairmanshift. However, hundreds of people from the whole country
      take their exams there, so without more clues it will be almost impossible
      to know who it was.\n \n The University has rejected providing a list of students,
      so unless the police can get a warrant, the interview process will be even
      more difficult.\n \n For the time being, we actually thank this man who freed
      the city from at least one unlawful and despicable human being."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 233674859155456
    m_Localized: "Looks like the thief murder we had a few nights ago was not an
      isolated case nor an accident. We have a vigilante among us. \n \n Last night,
      a group of thugs were planning some criminal activity that is still to be determined.
      They were roaming the house of Mrs. Scarlett in suspicious clothing and moving
      patterns.\n \n Mrs. Scarlett wasn\u2019t home, but her maid got scared and
      called the police. Turns out, when the police arrived, the thugs were beaten
      up and left crying on the street.\n \n According to the maid, she didn\u2019t
      see anything, after calling the police, she locked herself in the bathroom
      and prayed.\n \n Police are investigating the crime scene and trying to find
      any clues that can point to the suspect, although the community is pretty pleased
      with the vigilante not being even identified.\n \n The police ask anyone who
      has any info on what happened last night to call 555-8375-9821."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 233672007028736
    m_Localized: Someone is stopping crimes for good
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 233676738203648
    m_Localized: Is the vigilante getting sloppy?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 233678415925248
    m_Localized: "Last night, at the construction site, many construction workers/criminals
      were brutally beaten after a witness called the police upon hearing screams.\n
      \n The victim count was not precise by police yet, but we counted around 5.
      These guys were disguised as construction workers, or even actually working,
      but they had a double life or ulterior motive for being there.\n \n That site
      has a direct underground connection with the city\u2019s bank. Police think
      the men were digging a tunnel to do a huge heist, but were interrupted by a
      mysterious man in the middle of the night.\n \n According to the preliminary
      reports, the thieves were beaten with a wooden hammer and some greased half-prints
      were found in the scene. Is our vigilante about to be caught? We surely hope
      not!\n \n But as officials, we need to convey law and police regulations and
      let you know that if you have any information that may be significant, please
      call 555-8375-9821."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
